Reference implementation: https://github.com/arduino/arduino-modulino-mpy/tree/main/src/modulino
Difference between print() and uart.write(): https://forum.micropython.org/viewtopic.php?t=10304
Where do print statements send information from main.py?: https://forum.micropython.org/viewtopic.php?t=6253
Getting a MicroPython REPL prompt: https://docs.micropython.org/en/latest/esp8266/tutorial/repl.html

---------

Forward UART messages to "Virtualization Program" (VP). On ESP8266 we can use only the UART0, but it is allocated to REPL.
"Virtualization Program" might be able to provide a terminal on its side. The REPL on IDE would be disabled, but the user
can still interact through the VP.

In VP the user should be able to drag and drop Modulino modules, and address them as with the modulino library.

Input:
- Modulino Buttons: A three-button Modulino.
- Modulino Distance: Measure distance to an object.
- Modulino Movement: Measure acceleration and positioning.
- Modulino Knob: A rotating knob with a button.
- Modulino Thermo: Read surrounding temperature and humidity.

Output:
- Modulino Buzzer: A piezo speaker.
- Modulino Pixels: Control RGB LEDs on the Modulino Pixels.

Some modules should provide output, others should provide input (Buttons).
